# TypeScript Guidelines

The @10up/block-components library uses TypeScript for type safety and better developer experience.

## Types and Interfaces

- Use interfaces for object shapes that will be extended or implemented
- Use type aliases for unions, intersections, or simple object types
- Export interface and type definitions for public APIs
- Use descriptive names for types and interfaces
- Place shared types in separate files when used across multiple components

## Best Practices

- Use explicit return types for functions and methods
- Use proper typing for React props and state
- Define strong typing for WordPress data structures
- Use generics when appropriate for reusable components and functions
- Avoid `any` type when possible; use `unknown` instead when type is genuinely unknown
- Use type guards and type assertions when necessary

## WordPress-Specific Types

- Use types from `@wordpress` packages where available
- Use `wp-types` for additional WordPress type definitions
- For custom WordPress data, create appropriate interfaces

## Example Type Definitions

```typescript
// Component Props interface
export interface ContentPickerProps {
  label?: string;
  contentTypes?: string[];
  placeholder?: string;
  onPickChange?: (ids: any[]) => void;
  maxContentItems?: number;
  content?: any[];
}

// WordPress-specific types
import { Post } from '@wordpress/core-data';

// Generic types
export type SortableDirection = 'horizontal' | 'vertical';
```

